From a84bf55a28a10d61a80967e831b863f909d7483b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:09:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] cert: add DPP onboarding support for WFA certification mode

Add the agent/controller pieces needed to run the DPP certification
test cases through the UCC (CAPI) interface.

Agent:
- Move local DPP bootstrap key/URI generation from son_slave_thread
  into dpp_bootstrap_utils; expose it via the GetLocalBootstrap
  dev_exec_action, which now returns BootstrappingData.
- dev_set_config accepts "type,dpp" and switches onboarding to DPP;
  dev_reset_default reverts to WSC and clears stale DPP state
  (bootstrap, 1905 credentials/TK, wired session) so test cases can
  be repeated without a restart.
- Derive the PMKID with the 1905 PMK and put the matching RSNE in
  EAPOL-Key M2, as the hostapd Authenticator requires.
- Add SupportedService TLV to the BSS Configuration Request and
  accept the Supported Frequency Band TLV in AP-Autoconfiguration
  Search (observed from qca-ezmesh).
- Make the DPP config JSON parsing whitespace-tolerant and log it
  in chunks to avoid syslog truncation.

Controller:
- SetPeerBootstrap persists the peer URI to /etc/prplmesh/dpp_uri;
  dev_reset_default wipes peer URIs (keeping the local-agent line)
  and the forced DPP settings.
- Reject WSC M1 from remote agents when onboardingtype=DPP.
- In certification mode, emit cred.akm in name form (dpp+sae+psk)
  and include the DPP AKM selector.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
